 "text": "The word vaccine comes from a cow. 1700s England. Dr. Edward Jenner hears that milkmaids who catch cowpox, a mild disease from cows, don't seem to get deadly smallpox. May 1796. He takes material from a milkmaid's cowpox sore and puts it into a small cut on an eight-year-old boy, James Phipps. Weeks later, he exposes the boy to smallpox. James doesn't get sick. The Latin for cow is vacca. So we call it vaccination. Every legend has a beginning.",
